# Skelica — Frontend Environment Variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. Everything here is PUBLIC: Vite inlines any
# variable prefixed with VITE_ into the shipped JavaScript bundle, where anyone can read it.
#
# ⚠️  NEVER put an API key in a VITE_-prefixed variable. Doing so publishes the key to every
# visitor of the deployed site. (This file used to show exactly that, for both OpenAI and
# Anthropic. It was wrong.)
#
# Provider keys are not needed for this app to run. The optimizer clients in `src/llm/` read
# user-supplied keys from localStorage (Settings panel) — not from the environment — and they
# are not wired into the UI. Server-side keys would belong in Cloudflare Workers secrets.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Funnel analytics (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a provider configured every track() call is a console.debug no-op and nothing is
# sent anywhere. Events never include prompt content — only lengths, scores and grades.
#
# Option A — Plausible (cookieless, custom events):
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=plausible
# VITE_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=skelica.pages.dev
#
# Option B — Umami (self-hostable, cookieless, custom events):
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=umami
# VITE_ANALYTICS_SCRIPT_URL=https://your-umami-host/script.js
# VITE_ANALYTICS_WEBSITE_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
